import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"User-configured remote plugin markets","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/plugin-markets-episode.md","filePath":"records/plugin-markets-episode.md"}'),r={name:"records/plugin-markets-episode.md"};function o(n,e,d,c,l,h){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="user-configured-remote-plugin-markets" tabindex="-1">User-configured remote plugin markets <a class="header-anchor" href="#user-configured-remote-plugin-markets" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;User-configured remote plugin markets&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Observed on 2026-11-07 in Rho source after 0.5.6. This extends the independent <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/third-party-plugins#remote-plugin-markets">package channel</a>: a person can add a publisher&#39;s index, search its plugins, and install a selected immutable source. The functional plugin remains owned by Rho-plugins. No Core or scientific plugin code changed in this episode.</p><h2 id="the-flow-that-ran" tabindex="-1">The flow that ran <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-flow-that-ran" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The flow that ran&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A disposable project and owned Rho service ran in Chrome 156.0.8078.81 on macOS. A controlled loopback HTTP index served the real <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/../site/market/rho.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">YuLab Rho catalog</a>, allowing malformed JSON and HTTP 503 to be exercised. Package installation fetched the actual public Git source:</p><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-light vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>git+https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho-plugins.git#50d2427683e9077a5141b011c9696c51a00c90c5:plugins/semantic-figures</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The Plugins page rejected malformed JSON without retaining a source. Correcting the index made Semantic figures searchable with <code>clusterProfiler</code>, even though that word is absent from its native package description. Searching, listing and reopening made no further index requests and installed nothing.</p><p><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/main/docs/plugin-markets/search-before-install.png" alt="A market keyword finds the package before installation"></p><p>An explicit refresh received HTTP 503. Rho showed the error and kept the previous index digest and entries. Installing its saved selection fetched the fixed Git commit, checked id/version and opened the plugin&#39;s actual Interactive figures view. The installed package recorded its market origin and index digest. The later successful refresh cleared the error. The source controls remained reachable at 1440, 1024, 768 and 390 px; none of those views overflowed horizontally.</p><p><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/main/docs/plugin-markets/cached-index.png" alt="Failed refresh retains an installable saved index"></p><p>Removing the source kept the installed package, its digest and its searchable <code>clusterProfiler</code>/<code>cnetplot</code> keywords. No scientific runtime started: the test configured missing Core/R executables, and the service still reported no R sessions. This checks discovery, installation and opening the view. Native plot selection and linked plotting retain their separate <a href="/Rho/docs/records/semantic-figures-episode">semantic-figure evidence</a>.</p><h2 id="what-the-observations-changed" tabindex="-1">What the observations changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-observations-changed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What the observations changed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The first invalid-index run displayed a generic unknown-operation error because the new reader threw plain JavaScript errors. The owner now uses Rho&#39;s structured faults for invalid indexes, limits and unavailable sources. The same browser path then named invalid JSON and allowed correction in place.</p><p>The first removal implementation lost the market-only search words. Recording those keywords with the installed package&#39;s origin made the same search work after source removal. A repeat browser run checked both words and the retained package digest.</p><p>The new operation also needed an explicit top-level object schema for Rho&#39;s discovery projection. Its focused projection and HTTP/CLI checks pass. A broader all-operation adapter probe stopped at a missing-effect-contract refusal; that broad adapter path was not investigated further and is not claimed as passing.</p><h2 id="published-https-index" tabindex="-1">Published HTTPS index <a class="header-anchor" href="#published-https-index" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Published HTTPS index&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/main/site/market/rho.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">public index</a> was published in Rho commit <code>1be1be80</code>. A fresh disposable service added that exact URL through the CLI, then the browser found <code>clusterProfiler</code>, installed the fixed public Git package and opened Interactive figures. A second explicit refresh of the public URL succeeded. The full public URL and controls also fit the 390 px view without horizontal overflow. The returned package digest matched the controlled episode, and no scientific runtime started. This run also included the Plugins page changes from <code>7f923118</code>; the controlled failure/recovery episode was repeated on that combination afterward.</p><p><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/main/docs/plugin-markets/public-search.png" alt="The real HTTPS index, before installation"></p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/plugin-markets/public-report.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">public report</a> keeps the exact URL, index digest, package digest, timestamp and browser. Repeat with <code>node scripts/plugin-markets-public-episode.mjs</code>; this uses the real HTTPS and Git endpoints and closes its owned browser and service. Both episode scripts leave disposable state and evidence in their output folder for inspection.</p><h2 id="verification-and-limits" tabindex="-1">Verification and limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-and-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification and limits&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>npm run build</code> and <code>npm run check:contracts</code> passed.</li><li><code>node --test test/extension-markets.test.mjs test/extensions.test.mjs test/protocol.test.mjs test/validate.test.mjs</code>: 15 passed on the combined source, including 9 extension checks. These cover restart/cache behavior, invalid formats and sources, streamed size, entry/source/time limits, stale revisions and digests, actual staged package identity/version mismatches, CLI/API consistency and Agent authorization.</li><li>The existing entry-contract, contract-coverage, protocol, validation and layered MCP suites passed 16 checks before the final discovery-schema adjustment. The focused discovery check and current generated-contract check passed afterward.</li><li><code>node scripts/plugin-markets-episode.mjs</code>: six browser groups passed against the real public Git package. The <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/plugin-markets/report.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">retained report</a> records the exact installed digest, index digest, browser and viewport results. <code>RHO_MARKET_EPISODE</code> selects a disposable output folder; the script closes its browser, service and fixture server after the run.</li></ul><p>Both browser runs passed with no page errors. Screenshots were read after the combined run; the narrow layout wraps the source URL and stacks its controls. The four changed documentation pages were rendered and inspected, and the documentation build and link/assembly check passed. This pass does not establish independent-user usability, other OS behavior, registry publication, market signing, automatic updates, or installation into the person&#39;s running Rho. No npm release was made.</p>',22)])])}const m=t(r,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
